	(text "Revision 1a\n- Intial Revision\n- Layout Notes:\n- Shield GND may need to be split per connector instead of connected together.\n- Decide on number of expansion header pins based on space constraints.\n- Check USB3 ESD Protection signal ordering\nRevision 1b\n- Added 1M resistor to USB PHY clk\n- Added DNP pull up resistor to PS_POR_B for ES errata\n- Added current limiting resistors to:  PS_LED, PS_ERROR_OUT, PS_ERROR_STATUS, PGOOD, CC_PG, FMC_PG_C2M\n- Changed D19 LED from Red to Green\n- Updated DP ESD power supply\n- USBC power:  R244 DNP; R245 0 ohm; JP12 pin 1 is USBC_VBUS; Added capacitance on VBUS line\n- Removed PCIe connector / caps\n- Added USB3 connector / USB2 Hub\n- Updated LVDS connector\n- Added pull up resistor to USB3_DIR (A_B_SIDE) open drain output\n- Updated OSDZU3 power output current documentation\n- Added second footprint for QSPI Flash\n- Split fan header into two 2-pin headers (5V and 12V)\n- Changed GND_ANA resistors to 0603\n- Added Mikroe Click header (includes I2C ADC)\nRevision 1c:\n- Removed USB3 connector / USB2 Hub\n- Removed ability for board to act as a USB power sink (source only)\n- Updated footprint for MAC ID EEPROM\n- Updated spacing around USB-C ESD components\n- Updated footprint for NTE0506MC to allow for alternate parts\n- Moved large capacitors for USB-C\n- Changed MW jumper to input 5V\n- Added jumpers for UART0 / UART1\n- Added test points / jumpers around reset supervisor\n- Changed all BJT transistors to FETs\n- Updated capacitors / documentation around SYSMON circuit\n- Updated reset circuitry:  Changed PS_DONE LED to FET; Removed CC_RESET; Added LED for OSDZU3_RST\n- Changed Fan connectors to JST-XH\n- Added ZU3 control for TP STBY, RESET; Added control options for power / backlight\n- Fixed Touch Connector footprint\n- Added option to use 12V for VSUPPLY\n- Added jumper for PWR_EN\n- Moved LVDS connector to better fit mechancials for touch screen\nRevision 1d:\n- Connected TP_RST to ZU3 (JX2_HD_SE_11_N)\n- Fixed pinout of fan connector\n- Moved power supply of I2C GPIO Expander (TCA9534PWR) to 3.3V power rail.\n- Fixed footprint for U29 (MMSZ4679T1G)\n- Added J20.  SD/OE on clock chip set to 1 by default (clocks disabled); J20 must be installed for clocks to operate.\n- Updated J14 footprint\n- Increased current capacity of inductor L2\nRevision 1e:\n- Updated R134 value to reduce turn on time of output power transistors for USB-C\n- Added inverter between STUSB1600 output and input of high speed mux.\n- Added jumpers to isolate PMOD / Click shared pins\n- 11/16/2023:  Updates to docuemntation based on Production Datasheet"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
